    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20-a8">

                <pb facs="0116" n="20" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg20"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8 in No. 69.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tower to Mr. Guerra.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-25"><hi rendition="#italic">March 25,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have duly received your letter of the
                    25th of March, and I have already written to the Bezirkshauptmann in Hrastnig
                    about your case. I shall see that the American passport which you bear is
                    respected. At the same time I must inform you that the Department of State does
                    not encourage the return of naturalized American citizens to the country of
                    their birth; and it reserves the right to deny them its protection if they go
                    back there to take up their residence. You left America in the month of May,
                    1897, within four weeks after having <pb facs="0117" n="21" xml:id="pg21"/> been
                    naturalized, and, returning to your home in Hrastnig, you have lived there with
                    your parents for nearly a year.</p>
                <p>While you are claiming protection from the United States, and I am taking steps
                    now to give it to you, I wish you would tell me what your relations are to the
                    United States in return. Have you any interests there, and when do you intend to
                    return thither to perform your duties as a citizen? Do you pay taxes in
                    America?</p>
                <p>Awaiting your reply, I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charlemagne Tower.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
